00:06:01.653 --> 00:06:05.772
I have to speak to him personally. It's
not something you discuss on the phone.


00:06:05.991 --> 00:06:07.573
I need to see him.


00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:31.884
No.
No, definitely not.


00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:34.762
Please don't call him.
Don't tell him, OK?


00:06:38.607 --> 00:06:42.020
No, by carpool.
Flying is too expensive this late.


00:07:24.653 --> 00:07:27.395
Hi, it's Jan.
From "Share A Ride", yes.


00:07:27.572 --> 00:07:29.108
Where are you?


00:07:30.742 --> 00:07:33.154
What?


00:07:33.328 --> 00:07:36.070
On the website it said 5 p.m.!


00:07:36.456 --> 00:07:38.072
Wait...
No, wait!


00:07:38.249 --> 00:07:39.239
Hello!


00:08:19.416 --> 00:08:22.078
Are you heading west,
like to Cologne?


00:08:22.252 --> 00:08:23.492
Not at all, no.


00:08:23.712 --> 00:08:25.202
Ok, thanks.


00:08:38.977 --> 00:08:40.308
Hello.


00:08:41.354 --> 00:08:45.143
Are you heading to Cologne by chance?
- No, sorry. Hamburg.


00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:48.562
Thanks anyway.
Safe trip.


00:08:51.197 --> 00:08:52.779
Hello.


00:08:52.991 --> 00:08:54.948
Are you heading to Cologne?
- Yes, why?


00:08:55.118 --> 00:08:56.825
Could you give me a ride?


00:08:57.037 --> 00:08:58.823
No, sorry, we're full.


00:08:59.039 --> 00:09:01.030
No problem, thanks anyway.


00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:21.262
Are you heading to Cologne, by chance?


00:09:22.604 --> 00:09:23.765
Yes.


00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:26.438
Could you maybe give me a ride?


00:09:26.649 --> 00:09:29.437
I had a carpool, but they stood me up.


00:09:29.611 --> 00:09:31.978
Now I'm stuck here and...


00:09:32.781 --> 00:09:34.772
I'd throw in some gas money.


00:09:35.033 --> 00:09:37.024
Or motor oil.


00:09:42.332 --> 00:09:44.164
That's ok.
You can come along.


00:09:44.334 --> 00:09:46.075
Really? Cool!
- No problem.


00:09:46.252 --> 00:09:47.413
Great.


00:09:49.339 --> 00:09:51.876
I just need to wash my hands.


00:09:52.092 --> 00:09:53.127
O Kay-


00:09:53.259 --> 00:09:54.374
Just wait here, 0k?


00:09:54.552 --> 00:09:56.168
Perfect, thanks.


00:09:56.262 --> 00:09:58.424
See you.
- See you.


00:10:17.408 --> 00:10:19.240
Okay.
- All cleaned up?


00:10:23.706 --> 00:10:24.787
Jump in.


00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:27.833
Alright?
- Yeah, fine.


00:10:28.044 --> 00:10:30.331
You can sit here.


00:10:43.726 --> 00:10:45.763
Jule.
- Jan, hi.


00:11:01.452 --> 00:11:02.783
You hitchhike a lot?


00:11:03.872 --> 00:11:05.954
No, first time.


00:11:08.459 --> 00:11:12.544
Lucky me.
I asked two people before you.


00:11:12.755 --> 00:11:15.372
But they were full or headed elsewhere.


00:11:15.592 --> 00:11:17.333
And then you showed up.


00:11:18.136 --> 00:11:21.299
Cool ride!
Real nice.


00:11:21.431 --> 00:11:22.421
Thanks.


00:11:23.433 --> 00:11:25.049
It even has a fridge, right?


00:11:25.226 --> 00:11:27.433
Yeah, and an oven.


00:11:29.314 --> 00:11:32.056
What model is it?


00:11:32.775 --> 00:11:35.688
It's a Hymermobil
on a Mercedes 303 chassis.


00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:37.310
Cool.


00:11:37.447 --> 00:11:39.609
It's a bit older, right?


00:11:39.741 --> 00:11:41.857
No, brand-new.


00:11:42.702 --> 00:11:44.613
About 30.


00:11:45.038 --> 00:11:46.574
30 years old?


00:11:46.748 --> 00:11:49.035
You travel a lot in it?


00:11:49.209 --> 00:11:50.449
Not really, no.


00:11:50.543 --> 00:11:53.160
But it's yours.
- Yes.


00:11:53.338 --> 00:11:56.797
It used to belong to my brother.
- Okay.


00:11:57.383 --> 00:12:00.592
We traveled in it a lot,
but now it's mine.


00:12:01.095 --> 00:12:03.507
It "used to" belong to your brother?


00:12:04.224 --> 00:12:07.216
My brother...
He passed away two years ago.


00:12:08.645 --> 00:12:11.763
Shit.
I'm sorry.


00:12:12.565 --> 00:12:14.306
It's OK.


00:12:21.241 --> 00:12:23.653
Want a sip?
It's still cold.


00:12:23.743 --> 00:12:25.700
Sure.
- Shall I open it?


00:12:28.873 --> 00:12:29.954
Thanks.


00:12:33.962 --> 00:12:34.952
Elderflower?


00:12:36.297 --> 00:12:37.378
Homemade?
- Yep.


00:12:37.548 --> 00:12:38.879
Cool.


00:12:40.635 --> 00:12:43.502
Are you from Cologne?
- No, Berlin.


00:12:46.099 --> 00:12:48.636
So what are you doing in Cologne?


00:12:49.435 --> 00:12:54.145
Moving on. I'm taking a bus.
To Spain.


00:12:54.315 --> 00:12:55.897
Vacation?


00:12:56.609 --> 00:12:59.021
No, I'm...
visiting my father.


00:12:59.529 --> 00:13:01.440
He lives there?
- Exactly.


00:13:01.656 --> 00:13:03.442
In northern Spain.


00:13:05.076 --> 00:13:06.783
What do you do in Berlin?


00:13:07.829 --> 00:13:10.161
I study biology at the
Humboldt University.


00:13:10.331 --> 00:13:12.322
Cool.
- And you?


00:13:12.458 --> 00:13:15.246
I study, too.
Political science.


00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:18.333
Cool.
- Well, it's a lot of statistics.


00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:21.252
I sometimes envy you natural scientists.


00:13:21.342 --> 00:13:25.176
Theory, experiment, result:
that has such a nice clarity.


00:13:25.263 --> 00:13:27.095
Well, it's not that simple...


00:13:29.434 --> 00:13:32.552
I blew my biochemistry exam
this morning.


00:13:32.729 --> 00:13:34.595
I'd prefer not to talk about my studies.


00:13:34.772 --> 00:13:36.354
Sure, sorry.


00:13:42.363 --> 00:13:43.649
May I ask how old you are?


00:13:44.699 --> 00:13:46.189
24.


00:13:46.868 --> 00:13:49.075
And you?
- Me too.


00:13:50.538 --> 00:13:52.620
So we have three more years.


00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:55.623
Three years before what?
- Before we turn 27.


00:13:56.461 --> 00:13:58.748
When all cool people bail out.


00:13:59.589 --> 00:14:03.799
Kurt Cobain, Janis Joplin,
Amy Winehouse, Heath Ledger...


00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:05.500
You think so?


00:14:06.512 --> 00:14:10.176
Well, that's the saying.
Never heard of it?


00:14:13.853 --> 00:14:17.437
I'm totally against suicide,
if that's what you're thinking.


00:14:19.233 --> 00:14:23.227
It may sound strange,
but I think suicide's selfish.


00:14:23.654 --> 00:14:27.522
I mean, you've solved your own problems.


00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:30.112
But your relatives really suffer.


00:14:30.286 --> 00:14:35.452
An old friend killed himself seven years
ago and his mom still doesn't speak.


00:14:35.583 --> 00:14:39.247
Not a word. She just sits in her yard
and stares into space.


00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:41.002
She's totally done for.


00:14:41.172 --> 00:14:43.038
You think it's selfish.


00:14:43.383 --> 00:14:45.875
I beg your pardon,
but once you're in that place,


00:14:46.094 --> 00:14:47.584
you don't evenexistanymore.


00:14:47.762 --> 00:14:51.050
You can't think of others.
You can't think at all anymore.


00:14:51.182 --> 00:14:54.300
You just want it to stop.
- And it does stop.


00:14:54.435 --> 00:14:56.972
You've solved your problems.


00:14:57.146 --> 00:15:00.980
But you're not only responsible
for your own life.


00:15:01.609 --> 00:15:05.603
It's a fact: The relatives
suffer like hell.


00:15:06.572 --> 00:15:09.860
What are you babbling about?
You have no idea what you're saying.


00:15:10.076 --> 00:15:12.659
You have this attitude that
the media spreads...


00:15:12.829 --> 00:15:15.537
What?
- But you're just talking shit.


00:15:16.165 --> 00:15:20.079
Not true at all! I told you
that I witnessed it with a friend.


00:15:20.294 --> 00:15:23.036
His mother was so sweet,
and now she's a wreck.


00:15:23.214 --> 00:15:25.831
"So sweet."
And your friend, what about him?


00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:29.042
But I see the family, too.
They're completely ruined.


00:15:29.887 --> 00:15:31.673
That's so fucked up!


00:15:32.807 --> 00:15:35.390
No wonder you go to hell
for suicide in most religions.


00:15:35.852 --> 00:15:38.890
Is that so?
- As far as I know, yes.


00:15:48.322 --> 00:15:50.689
Sorry, I didn't mean to get to you...
- Stop it.


00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:00.832
I think this was a bad idea.


00:16:01.043 --> 00:16:03.876
I'm not really sociable at the moment.
I think...


00:16:05.089 --> 00:16:07.376
...you should maybe find another ride.


00:16:10.636 --> 00:16:12.627
<i>Sam!-
_ okay-</i>


00:16:13.431 --> 00:16:14.421
Illa:-


00:16:15.183 --> 00:16:17.550
I'll take the next exit.


00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:34.657
Her brother!


00:16:35.536 --> 00:16:37.743
Fuck!
Fuck...


00:16:41.834 --> 00:16:44.826
MY Phone.
No! Jule!


00:16:45.338 --> 00:16:46.624
Jule!


00:17:59.245 --> 00:18:03.284
Listen, I'm taking a pit
stop, I gotta take a nap.


00:18:03.416 --> 00:18:07.751
You can crash in the bottom bunk if
you like. - OK, cool. Great, thanks.


00:18:14.051 --> 00:18:16.213
No, everything's fine.


00:18:19.223 --> 00:18:21.089
I'm on my way to see you.


00:18:23.603 --> 00:18:25.219
Yeah, with the RV.


00:18:28.149 --> 00:18:29.765
Aren't you happy?


00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:36.271
Alex, I'll call you right back.


00:18:40.786 --> 00:18:41.776
Yes?


00:18:42.788 --> 00:18:46.031
I'm admiring your RV.


00:18:46.334 --> 00:18:48.416
We have an RV, too.


00:18:48.502 --> 00:18:52.040
It's practical. Room for the kids.
But your ride, it's just...


00:18:52.173 --> 00:18:53.334
...fantastic.


00:18:53.382 --> 00:18:55.168
A cult model!


00:18:56.802 --> 00:18:58.042
Thanks.


00:18:58.512 --> 00:18:59.877
I'm Torge.


00:19:00.306 --> 00:19:01.717
Hello. Jule.


00:19:02.558 --> 00:19:04.549
These are the original furnishings!


00:19:07.647 --> 00:19:08.887
Awesome.


00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:11.932
And the AC still works?


00:19:12.234 --> 00:19:14.271
No, hasn't for a long time.


00:19:15.821 --> 00:19:17.812
Do you have a glass of water for me?


00:19:18.866 --> 00:19:20.277
Sure, yeah.


00:19:39.095 --> 00:19:41.052
I'll go brush my teeth.
- Go ahead.


00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:45.849
And then in the other direction, right'?


00:19:50.439 --> 00:19:51.850
You're pretty.


00:19:55.319 --> 00:19:57.151
Can you please leave now.


00:19:58.406 --> 00:20:00.647
Why?
- Because I say so.


00:20:09.333 --> 00:20:10.448
You leave now.


00:20:11.627 --> 00:20:12.992
No.


00:20:13.421 --> 00:20:15.628
Leave or I'll call the police.


00:20:44.535 --> 00:20:45.821
You smell so good.


00:20:56.172 --> 00:20:57.412
Come here.


00:20:59.008 --> 00:21:00.590
Hands off!


00:21:02.595 --> 00:21:06.304
Jule, it's Jan. Can you open up?
I left my phone with you.


00:21:07.141 --> 00:21:09.223
Come in, it's open!


00:21:14.982 --> 00:21:16.893
Get out.


00:21:17.651 --> 00:21:20.143
Get out!
- Thanks for your hospitality.


00:21:20.321 --> 00:21:21.436
Piss off.


00:21:22.573 --> 00:21:24.985
Piss off!
- Have a nice evening.


00:21:25.826 --> 00:21:27.157
He has my phone.


00:21:29.580 --> 00:21:31.537
Give me the phone.
- Piss off!


00:21:40.841 --> 00:21:42.627
Stupid asshole, I'll kill you.


00:21:51.393 --> 00:21:52.303
Cunt!


00:21:52.561 --> 00:21:54.598
Piss off!


00:22:00.653 --> 00:22:02.018
Shit, are you OK?


00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:05.237
Wait, I'll get water.


00:22:16.335 --> 00:22:18.417
Yeah, take off, asshole!


00:22:22.049 --> 00:22:23.255
Open up.


00:22:24.093 --> 00:22:25.299
Alright?


00:22:29.515 --> 00:22:30.880
One more time, here.


00:22:31.058 --> 00:22:33.425
Sorry I sprayed you, too.
I panicked.


00:22:35.646 --> 00:22:39.514
At least you got that guy.
- Shit, your eyes are so red.


00:22:41.318 --> 00:22:43.150
So are yours.


00:22:43.320 --> 00:22:45.277
We look like zombies.


00:22:46.448 --> 00:22:48.655
You came out of nowhere.


00:22:50.244 --> 00:22:53.236
A truck driver picked me up.
I was sleeping in his truck.


00:22:53.330 --> 00:22:56.994
No way, what a coincidence.
If you hadn't shown up...


00:22:57.167 --> 00:22:58.498
Fuck.


00:23:00.337 --> 00:23:01.543
Eye drops?


00:23:08.095 --> 00:23:09.176
Alright?


00:23:09.263 --> 00:23:11.425
You know karate or something?


00:23:11.432 --> 00:23:13.014
A bit, yeah.


00:23:13.100 --> 00:23:16.434
So there was no need for the pepper spray.
- Yes, there was.


00:23:16.562 --> 00:23:18.428
Can you do me, too?
- Sure.


00:23:19.648 --> 00:23:21.559
He was pretty skilled.


00:23:21.650 --> 00:23:25.143
I think he knew martial arts.
Ex-soldier or something.


00:23:25.863 --> 00:23:27.399
Open your eyes.


00:23:27.823 --> 00:23:31.282
A frustrated ex-soldier.


00:23:32.036 --> 00:23:35.154
Exactly. Thrown out for
lack of intelligence.


00:23:35.247 --> 00:23:37.454
Couldn't find the trigger anymore.


00:23:42.546 --> 00:23:44.412
What an asshole.


00:23:45.382 --> 00:23:47.419
Did you see his shoes?


00:23:47.843 --> 00:23:51.427
Men in white socks and sandals,
let me tell you: They're the worst.


00:23:52.514 --> 00:23:54.175
I'll remember that.


00:24:01.649 --> 00:24:05.062
So you're on your way to Bilbao
to see your father.


00:24:06.654 --> 00:24:09.817
Does he work there?
Or are your parents divorced?


00:24:11.075 --> 00:24:14.864
No, I grew up with my stepfather and...


00:24:15.829 --> 00:24:20.073
...the guy in Bilbao is my biological father.
I've never met him.


00:24:21.627 --> 00:24:23.334
Wow.


00:24:24.964 --> 00:24:26.875
And why is that?
I mean...


00:24:27.633 --> 00:24:31.843
I didn't know that my stepfather
wasn't my real father until I was 17.


00:24:34.223 --> 00:24:36.885
And last month I asked my mother...


00:24:37.518 --> 00:24:40.636
...to put me in touch with
my biological father.


00:24:41.021 --> 00:24:43.262
Three days ago, he called.


00:24:43.565 --> 00:24:47.433
I was just watching a game show on TV.
Totally absurd.


00:24:47.653 --> 00:24:49.394
Crazy.


00:24:51.448 --> 00:24:52.984
And, I mean...


00:24:53.158 --> 00:24:57.072
...how did you find out? That
your stepfather isn't your father?


00:24:59.832 --> 00:25:01.869
Well...
- Long story?


00:25:02.459 --> 00:25:05.076
Yeah, kinda.
- OK. You don't need to...


00:25:08.173 --> 00:25:11.256
Sorry I threw you out this afternoon.


00:25:11.635 --> 00:25:12.875
It's just that...


00:25:13.053 --> 00:25:16.216
...my brother was really 27
when he committed suicide.


00:25:16.390 --> 00:25:18.381
So it's a sensitive topic for me.


00:25:18.517 --> 00:25:20.383
I figured.


00:25:21.228 --> 00:25:23.139
Sorry that I...


00:25:30.821 --> 00:25:32.311
Headache?


00:25:33.323 --> 00:25:36.691
Wanna smoke some weed?
To relax. I brought some.


00:25:37.578 --> 00:25:38.989
No, thanks.


00:25:39.079 --> 00:25:41.161
But you can if you want!
- No need.


00:25:41.874 --> 00:25:43.239
Beer's enough.


00:25:44.418 --> 00:25:46.830
I guess I'm just really tired.


00:25:49.840 --> 00:25:51.296
OK, then...


00:25:51.383 --> 00:25:52.873
...thanks for the beer.


00:25:53.510 --> 00:25:56.047
I'll let you get some sleep.
- Listen...


00:25:57.222 --> 00:26:00.635
Would you mind sleeping here tonight?


00:26:02.019 --> 00:26:05.011
You know, if this guy turns up again,
I'm a bit...


00:26:06.315 --> 00:26:09.853
No, sure. I can do that.
- Really? Great, that's...


00:26:10.027 --> 00:26:12.394
Thanks.
- Sure thing.


00:26:18.619 --> 00:26:22.988
Jule, sure you don't want the bed? I'm
the guest, I should sleep on the floor.


00:26:24.750 --> 00:26:28.493
In India, I slept on the floor
for six months. Without a mat.


00:26:29.421 --> 00:26:30.707
It's good here.


00:26:30.964 --> 00:26:32.625
Very comfortable.


00:26:34.176 --> 00:26:35.507
It's your back.


00:26:45.062 --> 00:26:46.973
Do you have a favorite dream?


00:26:47.022 --> 00:26:48.308
What?


00:26:48.398 --> 00:26:49.980
A favorite dream.


00:26:52.611 --> 00:26:56.980
Yes, flying. I love
to dream of flying.


00:26:57.116 --> 00:26:59.027
Really?
So do I!


00:26:59.743 --> 00:27:06.581
What, really?
You too fly at night?


00:27:07.334 --> 00:27:14.673
Yeah, over the city, with my arms set back.
Like Superman.


00:27:15.676 --> 00:27:20.716
I feel so super free then.
Everything is possible.


00:27:23.183 --> 00:27:25.891
And how do you take off?


00:27:27.062 --> 00:27:31.101
I usually jump off a table
or a wall or something.


00:27:31.692 --> 00:27:36.437
And then, shortly before I hit the
floor, I do a body twist...


00:27:36.613 --> 00:27:39.856
...turn on my stomach and fly away.


00:27:40.033 --> 00:27:43.617
With my arms close to the body,
like a ski jumper.


00:27:44.121 --> 00:27:45.407
Wicked.


00:27:51.670 --> 00:27:53.126
Have a nice flight.


00:27:53.255 --> 00:27:54.586
You, too.


00:28:43.096 --> 00:28:45.087
Hey!


00:28:45.140 --> 00:28:46.676
Good morning!
- Good morning.


00:28:47.517 --> 00:28:48.723
I thought you'd left already.


00:28:48.852 --> 00:28:50.843
Oh no, I just didn't wanna wake you up.


00:28:50.979 --> 00:28:55.394
I was having breakfast with Manni,
my trucker friend.


00:28:55.734 --> 00:28:56.724
Oh, okay.


00:29:02.407 --> 00:29:04.694
Did you dream of flying?


00:29:04.826 --> 00:29:07.659
No, unfortunately not.
And you?


00:29:07.663 --> 00:29:11.406
Neither.
We should have smoked that pot.


00:29:11.500 --> 00:29:13.491
Yeah, maybe.


00:29:17.422 --> 00:29:22.883
I gotta go. Manni has to reach Paris today.
- Right, OK.


00:29:23.720 --> 00:29:25.176
Thanks again.


00:29:25.764 --> 00:29:27.721
For yesterday.
- Sure thing.


00:29:30.060 --> 00:29:32.142
Well, take care then.
- You too.


00:29:32.312 --> 00:29:33.723
Good luck.


00:29:34.022 --> 00:29:36.730
Safe trip.
- You too.


00:29:37.943 --> 00:29:39.274
Bye.
- Ciao.


00:29:45.075 --> 00:29:48.613
Jan, hang on.
Could you come back for a sec?


00:29:52.249 --> 00:29:55.162
I could also take you a little further.


00:29:55.460 --> 00:29:57.076
Really?
- Yeah, sure.


00:29:57.379 --> 00:29:59.711
Well, great!
I'd love that!


00:29:59.840 --> 00:30:02.207
Unless you prefer to ride with Manni.


00:30:03.635 --> 00:30:05.421
<i>MannTs musk: taste...</i>


00:30:06.096 --> 00:30:07.177
No.


00:30:07.431 --> 00:30:09.843
Great.
- I'll grab my stuff.


00:30:10.100 --> 00:30:12.091
Cool. See you.
- See you.


00:30:19.651 --> 00:30:21.062
To the next leg, right?


00:30:21.528 --> 00:30:23.940
Let's see how many miles
we last this time.


00:30:29.036 --> 00:30:31.198
Do you mind taking country roads?


00:30:31.371 --> 00:30:33.703
Not at all, I'm not in a hurry.


00:30:47.220 --> 00:30:50.554
Look, there's a stork!
It's really pretty.


00:30:58.231 --> 00:31:01.223
So where are you heading?
You haven't told me yet.


00:31:01.443 --> 00:31:03.525
Oh, right.
To Portugal.


00:31:03.695 --> 00:31:05.811
Portugal?
Wow. Pretty far.


00:31:05.989 --> 00:31:07.104
Yes.


00:31:07.199 --> 00:31:08.735
I'm visiting someone.


00:31:09.409 --> 00:31:10.524
Your father too?


00:31:11.036 --> 00:31:12.197
No.


00:31:13.413 --> 00:31:14.744
My boyfriend.


00:31:16.208 --> 00:31:18.745
He's doing his PhD there, in Tamera.


00:31:19.419 --> 00:31:21.831
What's it on?
- Ecological agriculture.


00:31:22.047 --> 00:31:24.539
Permacultures, water retention systems, etc...


00:31:24.549 --> 00:31:26.540
Water retention systems?


00:31:28.220 --> 00:31:31.429
Not just using water,
but keeping it in the cycle.


00:31:31.556 --> 00:31:34.139
Want the details?
- Some other time.


00:31:39.439 --> 00:31:41.430
May I?
- Sure.


00:31:46.405 --> 00:31:49.864
Absurd, right?
Two tons of steel to move one person?


00:31:50.826 --> 00:31:54.364
In 90% of the cars,
there's only one person.


00:31:54.454 --> 00:31:56.195
True.
Like me.


00:31:57.040 --> 00:31:58.530
Almost.


00:32:01.837 --> 00:32:03.202
And you?


00:32:03.380 --> 00:32:05.747
Lone wolf or social animal?


00:32:07.676 --> 00:32:10.759
Social animal, definitely!
Extremely social!


00:32:12.973 --> 00:32:17.137
No, neither one. Some friends,
some acquaintances, the usual.


00:32:18.437 --> 00:32:20.394
Leaning towards the lone wolf, maybe.


00:32:22.190 --> 00:32:24.852
You know how many people
in Germany live alone?


00:32:26.194 --> 00:32:28.185
No idea. 20%?
- 50%.


00:32:28.363 --> 00:32:30.195
Crazy.
- Yeah, right?


00:32:30.699 --> 00:32:34.363
And you know what?
I think there's a strategy behind it.


00:32:34.578 --> 00:32:35.739
Really?


00:32:36.580 --> 00:32:38.947
Economic reasons.
- "Economic reasons."


00:32:39.374 --> 00:32:40.455
Yes.


00:32:40.750 --> 00:32:42.115
Look:


00:32:42.377 --> 00:32:45.210
Take four people who
live in four apartments.


00:32:45.380 --> 00:32:49.339
They need four fridges, four vacuum
cleaners, four kettles, four...


00:32:49.759 --> 00:32:50.749
Flat screen TVs.


00:32:50.886 --> 00:32:54.504
Exactly! If they lived together,
they'd only need one of each.


00:32:54.681 --> 00:32:58.970
So economically it makes more sense if they
live alone, as they consume more.


00:32:59.186 --> 00:33:04.181
A friend wrote his thesis on that:
"Capitalism's Separation Strategy."


00:33:04.399 --> 00:33:06.515
That does sound like a thesis.


00:33:07.194 --> 00:33:10.186
But being alone is against
human nature, totally!


00:33:10.780 --> 00:33:13.397
Humans are social creatures!
Within minutes...


00:33:13.533 --> 00:33:15.945
...of being alone, we
secrete stress hormones!


00:33:16.203 --> 00:33:18.410
Cortisol and such.
- Wow.


00:33:19.748 --> 00:33:25.209
And Cortisol weakens the immune system,
so being alone makes you sick.


00:33:28.215 --> 00:33:30.047
But that's what they want.


00:33:30.217 --> 00:33:31.503
What?


00:33:31.676 --> 00:33:35.169
Us to be unhappy, so we consume more.


00:33:36.806 --> 00:33:40.390
You keep saying "they,"
but who are "they" supposed to be?


00:33:40.560 --> 00:33:45.851
Executives and politicians
who meet in dark rooms and decide...


00:33:45.982 --> 00:33:50.522
"Let's isolate them, so they consume
more and cease to resist."


00:33:51.947 --> 00:33:53.529
You can't seriously believe that.


00:33:53.698 --> 00:33:56.360
Well, I used to.
- And now?


00:33:56.535 --> 00:34:00.199
Now I think it's inherent to the system.
- Inherent to the system?


00:34:00.413 --> 00:34:05.999
Yes. Capitalism inevitably leads to
isolation - due to its fundamental principles.


00:34:07.128 --> 00:34:11.372
"The Fundamental Principles of Capitalism."
- Yeah, think about it:


00:34:11.383 --> 00:34:15.547
From a young age we're taught
to compete with each other.


00:34:15.762 --> 00:34:20.051
It starts in school. Who's the best-looking?
Who's the smartest? And so on...


00:34:20.183 --> 00:34:23.346
Life has become a permanent audition!


00:34:23.436 --> 00:34:26.554
1000 people apply to a
college, only ten get in.


00:34:26.565 --> 00:34:29.557
100 people apply for an
apartment, one gets it.


00:34:29.693 --> 00:34:33.561
You have to be tougher,
quicker and stronger 24/7!


00:34:33.572 --> 00:34:34.983
What a stress!


00:34:35.198 --> 00:34:37.735
Well, life's no day at the beach.


00:34:38.034 --> 00:34:41.026
Not in capitalism that's for sure.


00:34:43.623 --> 00:34:46.741
But that's just how it is:
Competition is in our blood.


00:34:46.960 --> 00:34:50.874
Take two kids running across a field:
One will always try to run faster.


00:34:52.215 --> 00:34:56.709
How is that related? - It totally
is! It starts there, in that field!


00:34:57.220 --> 00:34:59.427
We just LOVE competing.


00:34:59.556 --> 00:35:03.140
Competition is fun!
Even jungle warriors compete.


00:35:03.351 --> 00:35:06.764
But it's become so extreme!
Nonstop struggle and competition...


00:35:06.980 --> 00:35:09.347
The whole world has become
a damn Circus Maximus!


00:35:09.524 --> 00:35:10.605
You're exaggerating.


00:35:10.775 --> 00:35:16.942
What? The top 5% who own the capital
benefit from the rest scurrying about.


00:35:17.198 --> 00:35:21.442
Everyone else just works their asses off,
is unhappy and totally stressed out.


00:35:27.125 --> 00:35:29.287
That's not so nice, yeah.


00:35:29.377 --> 00:35:31.744
But that's nature's way.


00:35:31.755 --> 00:35:33.871
The hard in the garden,
the tender in the pond.


00:35:34.049 --> 00:35:36.211
The strongest survive, these
are the rules of evolution.


00:35:36.217 --> 00:35:37.753
Says who?


00:35:37.844 --> 00:35:38.834
Says Darwin.


00:35:39.012 --> 00:35:40.753
Darwin?
- Yes.


00:35:42.223 --> 00:35:45.682
Whoa, I don't think
you're up to date there.


00:35:47.520 --> 00:35:51.514
Oh, fuck...
I feel sick.


00:35:54.152 --> 00:35:55.517
I'm getting off the road.


00:36:13.046 --> 00:36:15.834
Oh shit, are you okay?


00:36:17.634 --> 00:36:19.841
Have another sip of water.


00:36:23.515 --> 00:36:25.506
Oh, shit.


00:36:30.271 --> 00:36:31.386
Are you all right?


00:36:31.564 --> 00:36:34.147
I hope it's not a sunstroke.
Are you dizzy?


00:36:34.317 --> 00:36:37.651
No, it's alright, I guess I just
ate something wrong.


00:36:37.821 --> 00:36:39.311
Alright


00:36:39.447 --> 00:36:43.532
I hope it's not because of
my pro-capitalist arguments.


00:36:43.660 --> 00:36:45.867
No, don't worry.


00:36:49.082 --> 00:36:51.119
I already feel better.
I'll wipe off my vomit.


00:36:51.251 --> 00:36:53.333
No, no.
Let me do that.


00:36:53.420 --> 00:36:55.331
You want to clean off my vomit?


00:36:55.422 --> 00:36:58.255
I was a civil servant in
oncology, I'll manage.


00:36:58.383 --> 00:36:59.669
O Kay-


00:37:01.010 --> 00:37:02.000
Oh, sorry.


00:37:02.137 --> 00:37:06.722
All good.
Say, can we go for a walk?


00:37:07.183 --> 00:37:11.893
Yeah, sure. Look, there's a
forest back there, a forest walk?


00:37:15.942 --> 00:37:20.436
The strongest survive. It's always
been like that. Darwin proved it.


00:37:20.780 --> 00:37:22.270
No, Jan.


00:37:22.407 --> 00:37:26.275
Darwin said "survival of the
fittest", not "survival of the strongest".


00:37:26.411 --> 00:37:29.745
Not the strongest survive,
but those who adapt best.


00:37:30.457 --> 00:37:34.997
It can also be the most bizarre.
Take the peacock for example.


00:37:35.128 --> 00:37:38.041
<i>The peacock'?
- Yes. Pave Cflstakus.</i>


00:37:38.298 --> 00:37:39.538
Peacock!


00:37:42.552 --> 00:37:46.887
If only the strong survive, why is there
a bizarre animal like the peacock?


00:37:47.056 --> 00:37:50.640
It's neither fast nor strong,
can't even run away.


00:37:51.603 --> 00:37:54.265
But it can spread it's tail
to a wonderful fan.


00:37:54.439 --> 00:37:56.976
The ladies love it, so it has more babies.


00:37:57.942 --> 00:38:02.277
See? In this case not the strongest survived,
but the most bizarre.


00:38:02.405 --> 00:38:03.816
There are so many examples.


00:38:04.073 --> 00:38:07.862
This "struggle for existence" is
total bullshit.


00:38:08.578 --> 00:38:11.616
Darwin was abused by the capitalists.


00:38:11.748 --> 00:38:13.409
From the beginning.


00:38:20.089 --> 00:38:22.046
But then what about gorillas?


00:38:22.300 --> 00:38:25.167
Gorillas fight until only one is left:


00:38:25.261 --> 00:38:26.797
The alpha male.


00:38:26.888 --> 00:38:31.553
Only the alpha male may reproduce.
It even kills the other males' babies.


00:38:31.810 --> 00:38:33.300
And we're all gorillas, or what?


00:38:33.561 --> 00:38:37.350
No, but human society works similarly.


00:38:37.607 --> 00:38:42.568
We fight until a pecking order is created.
And our economic system accommodates that.


00:38:42.779 --> 00:38:47.114
That's why it's the only one that works,
and why communism didn't work.


00:38:47.283 --> 00:38:50.867
Objection. Firstly, communism
was a hierarchical system too.


00:38:51.037 --> 00:38:55.782
And why? Because everyone wanted
the biggest piece of the cake!


00:38:55.875 --> 00:38:59.413
That's why "real socialism" never existed.


00:38:59.587 --> 00:39:02.750
Neither in East Germany,
nor in Russia, nor in China.


00:39:02.841 --> 00:39:06.835
Mao and Stalin forced a system on
the people that they didn't want.


00:39:07.011 --> 00:39:09.173
Because it doesn't fit human nature.


00:39:09.347 --> 00:39:13.341
Oh, please don't start with
"communism vs capitalism"...


00:39:13.434 --> 00:39:16.677
<i>Thais so 90s
Both systems suck.</i>


00:39:16.771 --> 00:39:20.264
The question of the basic principle
is much more interesting.


00:39:20.567 --> 00:39:23.104
What advances mankind more?


00:39:23.361 --> 00:39:25.102
Competition or cooperation?


00:39:25.280 --> 00:39:26.770
Competition.
- Cooperation.


00:39:27.073 --> 00:39:29.986
Competition. - Cooperation!
Why else did I give you a ride?


00:39:30.118 --> 00:39:31.654
And why did you kick me out?


00:39:32.370 --> 00:39:36.079
Come on, you know why. I took you
'cos I felt sorry for you.


00:39:36.207 --> 00:39:39.074
What??
You felt sorry for me??


00:39:39.210 --> 00:39:43.420
Never heard of compassion,
empathy, mirror neurons?


00:39:43.673 --> 00:39:48.292
You were sad. I saw that, felt what
you felt, and got sad, as well.


00:39:48.553 --> 00:39:53.263
Empathy! That's why I gave you a ride!
And that's the basis of humanity!


00:39:53.349 --> 00:39:57.889
It generates cooperation, which isn't
just nice, but the secret of our success!


00:39:58.062 --> 00:40:02.351
Thanks to cooperation, we descend
from Cro-Magnons, not Neanderthals.


00:40:04.611 --> 00:40:06.101
Wanna hear more?
- No.


00:40:06.279 --> 00:40:07.690
Sure you do.
- No!


00:40:08.072 --> 00:40:09.779
Stop it, I'm a gorilla!


00:40:12.702 --> 00:40:17.287
They lived at the end of the last Ice Age,
around 25,000 years ago.


00:40:17.582 --> 00:40:20.449
In southern France alongside
the Neanderthals.


00:40:20.960 --> 00:40:24.294
The Cro-Magnons survived,
while the Neanderthals went extinct.


00:40:24.380 --> 00:40:25.836
Know why?


00:40:26.090 --> 00:40:28.798
They killed the Neanderthals?
- No.


00:40:29.260 --> 00:40:31.092
Because of battue.


00:40:31.429 --> 00:40:38.426
It was like this: Neanderthals were lone
wolves who lived in groups of eight to ten.


00:40:38.561 --> 00:40:42.270
They fought each other,
and were massive, brawny beings.


00:40:42.357 --> 00:40:44.564
Like me.
- More or less.


00:40:44.692 --> 00:40:48.651
They needed around 5,000 calories
per day, a lot of meat.


00:40:49.113 --> 00:40:50.569
Like me.


00:40:51.449 --> 00:40:54.191
Yeah, maybe, anyway...


00:40:54.369 --> 00:40:58.738
At the end of the Ice Age, food became
scarce and they started eating each other.


00:40:59.457 --> 00:41:03.667
They were cannibals? - In the end.
Then they starved and went extinct.


00:41:03.795 --> 00:41:05.786
Now the Cro-Magnons:


00:41:06.089 --> 00:41:09.127
They lived in groups of up to 400.


00:41:09.425 --> 00:41:12.008
Together , they drove
animals towards cliffs...


00:41:12.136 --> 00:41:14.423
...who panicked and fell off them.
Et voila:


00:41:14.555 --> 00:41:18.093
They had loads of meat.
Real barbecue parties. - Cool.


00:41:18.351 --> 00:41:22.060
Having so much food
gave them time to paint caves.


00:41:22.438 --> 00:41:25.430
Their tongues developed,
they started talking.


00:41:25.608 --> 00:41:27.565
As the first homo sapiens.


00:41:27.694 --> 00:41:31.187
And from the Cro-Magnons we descend.
They're our ancestors.


00:41:31.364 --> 00:41:33.105
Really?
- Yes.


00:41:34.117 --> 00:41:37.200
They survived because
they cooperated...


00:41:37.370 --> 00:41:41.329
...while Neanderthals went extinct.
Battue, that was the success factor!


00:41:41.457 --> 00:41:46.827
So the social element was the
decisive factor in enabling humanity!


00:41:46.838 --> 00:41:50.877
And now the capitalists want to turn us
back into Neanderthals, get it?


00:41:51.342 --> 00:41:54.630
That's a bit one-sided, Jule.
- No, it isn't.


00:41:55.346 --> 00:41:58.964
Capitalism is an inhuman,
misanthropic system.


00:41:59.100 --> 00:42:03.264
It benefits the 1% at the top,
while the rest of humanity feels miserable.


00:42:03.354 --> 00:42:05.345
Sorry, but that's total bullshit.


00:42:05.440 --> 00:42:08.273
You act like humans are
peace-loving hippies...


00:42:08.359 --> 00:42:11.272
...who give out hugs
all day, but they're not.


00:42:12.572 --> 00:42:16.440
Know what they found on Otzi,
that iceman from 5,000 years ago? An ax.


00:42:16.659 --> 00:42:19.651
Not a peace pipe, an ax.
- Maybe he was felling trees.


00:42:20.371 --> 00:42:22.203
It was a battle ax, for killing.


00:42:22.623 --> 00:42:26.491
He had war injuries
and an arrow tip in his shoulder.


00:42:26.627 --> 00:42:29.210
That tip severed an artery
and he bled to death.


00:42:29.338 --> 00:42:33.206
He was murdered from behind
with a bow and arrow. Bang!


00:42:33.801 --> 00:42:37.510
That's what I see when I look at
5,000 years of human history:


00:42:37.597 --> 00:42:40.680
Murder and destruction.
People slitting throats.


00:42:40.808 --> 00:42:44.972
Tribal genocide, nations attacking
each other, hate, the Holocaust...


00:42:45.063 --> 00:42:50.024
...oppression. The history of
mankind is one big bloodbath!


00:42:51.360 --> 00:42:54.728
Every 3 seconds there's a murder
in the world. Every 3 seconds!


00:42:55.156 --> 00:42:59.650
Right now, a man stabs his wife
because she wants to leave him.


00:43:02.955 --> 00:43:04.537
We're not just good, Jule.


00:43:04.665 --> 00:43:08.875
We're evil, too.
- Evil.


00:43:10.338 --> 00:43:13.672
What about the guy who almost raped you.
Did he want to cooperate?


00:43:13.800 --> 00:43:16.258
What? You don't have to get polemical!


00:43:16.302 --> 00:43:19.090
What's that got to do with anything?
That was a troubled, stupid asshole.


00:43:19.180 --> 00:43:22.423
Of course there are people like that.
What fucking argument is that anyway?


00:43:27.063 --> 00:43:30.146
We're talking about
basic human traits.


00:43:30.316 --> 00:43:32.523
Those that promote us as humanity.


00:43:34.070 --> 00:43:41.033
Okay. And what about envy and greed?
Aren't these also basic human traits?


00:43:41.327 --> 00:43:46.117
If I eat potatoes every day, but my
neighbour has grilled chicken...


00:43:46.290 --> 00:43:49.499
...isn't it the rule rather than the
exception that I want chicken, too?


00:43:50.044 --> 00:43:53.662
Or if someone walks to work for ten
kilometers, while his neighbour...


00:43:53.798 --> 00:43:57.336
...goes by bike, isn't it normal and
humane that he also wants a bike?


00:43:57.510 --> 00:43:59.968
Yes, but this has nothing to do with envy.
It's just unfair.


00:43:59.971 --> 00:44:01.086
They should both have a bike.


00:44:01.180 --> 00:44:02.841
No, we're going around in circles here.


00:44:02.974 --> 00:44:05.136
He should save until he
can afford a bicycle...


00:44:05.309 --> 00:44:07.425
...for that he'll work harder and produce
better products or...


00:44:07.436 --> 00:44:09.677
...tomatoes or whatever he produces.


00:44:11.315 --> 00:44:16.105
"My bike","your bike"...
it all started much earlier.


00:44:16.237 --> 00:44:18.319
With the invention of property.


00:44:18.447 --> 00:44:21.735
If I don't own anything,
you can't envy me, can you?


00:44:21.951 --> 00:44:25.364
Look, nomads, they shared.
They shared everything.


00:44:25.538 --> 00:44:29.782
We love to share. Our body releases tons
of happiness hormones when we share.


00:44:29.792 --> 00:44:30.782
We love it.


00:44:32.295 --> 00:44:33.956
Then why don't we do it?


00:44:34.839 --> 00:44:38.002
I'm really hungry.
Shall we cook something?


00:44:38.176 --> 00:44:39.337
Yes.
- Yes?


00:44:39.510 --> 00:44:41.968
Definitely.
Chicken, perhaps?


00:44:42.054 --> 00:44:43.840
For you, only potatoes.


00:44:44.640 --> 00:44:46.301
No, I need meat.
Meeeeeat!


00:44:46.434 --> 00:44:48.846
Then go hunt a deer.


00:44:49.520 --> 00:44:54.356
I need you for that. For the battue.
- Forget it. Take a spade.


00:45:06.871 --> 00:45:12.537
It's great to add two or three
sprigs of rosemary.


00:45:26.891 --> 00:45:28.848
How's it going there?


00:45:29.602 --> 00:45:31.013
Thanks, I'm gettin into it.


00:45:32.605 --> 00:45:34.141
Still some dirt here.


00:45:37.860 --> 00:45:40.192
And there's also pretty much here.


00:45:40.613 --> 00:45:41.819
Get away!


00:45:54.335 --> 00:45:56.076
Next stop: Dortmund.


00:45:56.837 --> 00:45:59.169
All crazy Jans please disembark.


00:46:01.968 --> 00:46:04.835
Driving, driving, driving
down the Autobahn!


00:46:24.699 --> 00:46:26.610
Look, the Cologne Cathedral!


00:46:26.701 --> 00:46:29.113
Cologne!
- Carnival!


00:46:43.092 --> 00:46:46.835
Just drop me off at the corner,
I'll walk to the station from there.


00:46:47.680 --> 00:46:49.011
And then you'll take the bus?


00:46:51.517 --> 00:46:53.303
Just as I was getting used to you.


00:46:54.103 --> 00:46:57.812
Plus, I still have to convince you that
humans aren't as bad as you think.


00:46:58.024 --> 00:47:00.516
Well, that's true of course.


00:47:01.861 --> 00:47:03.772
Another 300 miles?


00:47:05.614 --> 00:47:06.945
Uhm, yeah!


00:47:07.033 --> 00:47:08.740
Sure, I'd love that.


00:47:09.368 --> 00:47:11.359
But only if it's not out of pity.


00:47:12.580 --> 00:47:14.947
No, don't worry.
Deal?


00:47:15.041 --> 00:47:16.327
Deal.


00:47:31.098 --> 00:47:32.179
Hey, look.


00:47:32.892 --> 00:47:34.974
Hello, Belgium!


00:47:35.519 --> 00:47:36.975
Bye, Germany!


00:47:40.066 --> 00:47:43.900
Wanna pick something from the
camping guide?


00:47:44.862 --> 00:47:47.069
"RV Camping Guide."


00:47:47.323 --> 00:47:48.609
This looks good:


00:47:48.699 --> 00:47:53.819
"The camping site Champe le Monde
lies in the midst of the hilly Ardennes."


00:47:58.501 --> 00:48:00.959
They're open.
- They are?


00:48:01.420 --> 00:48:03.957
From happy lambs?
- Yes, very happy-


00:48:06.967 --> 00:48:08.298
Meat!


00:48:08.969 --> 00:48:11.051
Shouldn't we grill it first?
- No!


00:48:26.612 --> 00:48:28.523
You OK or you need help?


00:48:28.614 --> 00:48:29.945
I'll manage.


00:48:41.377 --> 00:48:42.583
And?


00:48:43.170 --> 00:48:44.786
Looking good!


00:48:48.717 --> 00:48:50.128
Want some wine, too?


00:48:50.302 --> 00:48:51.963
Uhm, no.


00:48:52.096 --> 00:48:53.586
You don't drink?


00:48:53.722 --> 00:48:55.304
Not right now, no.


00:48:58.686 --> 00:49:00.347
Hunger, for example.


00:49:01.981 --> 00:49:07.067
There's so much wheat that we could
feed the world's population twice .


00:49:07.820 --> 00:49:10.733
It's just not being
distributed properly. Or...


00:49:10.948 --> 00:49:14.942
Wait, I wanna show you something.


00:49:18.330 --> 00:49:21.539
That red spot...
This area would be sufficient...


00:49:21.542 --> 00:49:24.079
...to supply the whole earth
with solar energy.


00:49:24.211 --> 00:49:25.701
The sun is that strong.


00:49:26.338 --> 00:49:30.047
Instead, we burn oil
and heat up our planet.


00:49:33.179 --> 00:49:36.422
Are you sure?
- Yes, it's all been calculated.


00:49:38.601 --> 00:49:40.842
And the map is always with you?


00:49:42.313 --> 00:49:47.353
It reminds me of what we could do, if
we'd just organize ourselves. Cooperate.


00:49:48.903 --> 00:49:52.021
Which we don't.
- Not yet.


00:49:58.537 --> 00:50:01.575
Are you nervous about
meeting your father?


00:50:02.166 --> 00:50:03.622
No, not at all.


00:50:04.168 --> 00:50:05.784
I'm looking forward to it.


00:50:07.713 --> 00:50:09.954
Want to hear the rest of the story?


00:50:10.174 --> 00:50:12.131
How I found out?


00:50:12.426 --> 00:50:13.712
Yes, I'd love to.


00:50:18.807 --> 00:50:22.095
Well, my father...
He...


00:50:22.394 --> 00:50:25.102
...never really knew
what to do with me.


00:50:25.231 --> 00:50:29.646
He never even hid his dislike.
I always asked myself why...


00:50:30.402 --> 00:50:33.110
...why he didn't like me, but...
Well...


00:50:34.448 --> 00:50:39.443
Then one summer day, we had this family
celebration at my grandmother's.


00:50:39.453 --> 00:50:41.319
I was 17.


00:50:41.956 --> 00:50:45.699
Everyone was there:
my older brother with his two kids...


00:50:45.709 --> 00:50:47.416
I have an older brother.


00:50:47.586 --> 00:50:49.418
His wife...


00:50:49.547 --> 00:50:51.788
Grandparents, uncles and aunties...


00:50:51.882 --> 00:50:53.498
The whole shebang.


00:50:54.176 --> 00:50:56.213
So I'm sitting there...


00:50:56.971 --> 00:51:00.805
...looking around. Everyone's
enjoying themselves, having fun.


00:51:03.102 --> 00:51:06.811
Suddenly I realize something's missing.
Something's wrong.


00:51:06.981 --> 00:51:10.224
Like a part of me's missing,
something in me is empty, you know?


00:51:10.401 --> 00:51:13.393
Inside of me it was getting
darker and darker.


00:51:14.321 --> 00:51:16.779
So I'm looking at my father's relatives...


00:51:17.408 --> 00:51:19.024
And suddenly...


00:51:19.159 --> 00:51:21.321
All of a sudden, it clicks.


00:51:21.537 --> 00:51:25.246
I realize what my problem is,
I get up, approach my mother and say:


00:51:25.416 --> 00:51:27.703
"He's not my father, right?"


00:51:29.336 --> 00:51:30.417
In front of everyone?


00:51:31.338 --> 00:51:32.794
In front of everyone.


00:51:33.716 --> 00:51:36.504
And your mother'?
How did she react?


00:51:36.969 --> 00:51:40.303
She said nothing at all.
Which was the answer, of course.


00:51:41.765 --> 00:51:46.384
Thus it was clear why he had
treated me like shit for 17 years.


00:51:50.858 --> 00:51:54.817
Is it my fault that my mother had
good taste for once in her life...


00:51:55.112 --> 00:51:57.399
by falling for a Spanish boatbuilder.


00:51:58.449 --> 00:52:00.406
A Spanish boatbuilder?


00:52:01.702 --> 00:52:04.660
1993, on vacation.
A one-night stand.


00:52:05.122 --> 00:52:07.489
My stepfather wanted her to
abort, but she refused.


00:52:07.666 --> 00:52:11.125
And so one fine day
I saw the light of the world.


00:52:49.792 --> 00:52:51.658
No?
- No, one more time.


00:52:51.794 --> 00:52:53.705
Yes, okay...


00:52:53.837 --> 00:52:55.373
Get back, it should be fine now.


00:52:55.506 --> 00:52:56.996
Really?
- Yes.


00:52:57.716 --> 00:52:58.706
Got it?


00:53:00.844 --> 00:53:02.505
Wow.
Alright?


00:53:03.389 --> 00:53:04.845
Really cool.


00:53:09.228 --> 00:53:10.434
Jan?


00:53:10.604 --> 00:53:12.436
Are you still awake?


00:53:12.606 --> 00:53:13.812
Yes.


00:53:15.609 --> 00:53:18.101
I'm really happy you're with me.


00:53:20.322 --> 00:53:22.689
I'd have gone crazy on my own.


00:53:23.742 --> 00:53:25.403
And gotten the flu.


00:53:26.203 --> 00:53:27.409
The flu?


00:53:28.163 --> 00:53:30.370
Yeah, being alone,
cortisol and all:


00:53:30.457 --> 00:53:32.539
Doesn't that weaken the immune system?


00:53:32.668 --> 00:53:34.409
That's true.


00:53:39.299 --> 00:53:43.167
One gentle touch kills thousands
of stress hormones, by the way.


00:53:43.303 --> 00:53:44.714
Really?


00:53:46.849 --> 00:53:49.682
I have to remember that.
- Do that.


00:53:53.689 --> 00:53:54.804
Good night.


00:53:55.691 --> 00:53:57.147
Good night.


00:54:30.392 --> 00:54:32.724
Look, we're almost in France!


00:54:33.854 --> 00:54:35.390
Bye bye. Belgium!


00:54:35.606 --> 00:54:37.813
Hello, France!


00:54:43.405 --> 00:54:45.646
Looks different right away, right?


00:54:45.741 --> 00:54:48.324
Yeah, and much less traffic, right?


00:55:19.858 --> 00:55:21.314
Alex?


00:55:21.860 --> 00:55:24.101
Hi, yes, it's me.


00:55:25.405 --> 00:55:26.941
I have to tell you something.


00:55:36.834 --> 00:55:41.829
I did want to tell you face to face,
but I couldn't stand it any longer, sorry.


00:55:44.174 --> 00:55:45.790
I have to go now.


00:55:47.386 --> 00:55:51.129
I'll call back, OK?
Bye.


00:56:05.821 --> 00:56:07.403
Are you OK?


00:56:08.156 --> 00:56:09.521
So-so.


00:56:10.701 --> 00:56:12.317
Can I help you?


00:56:12.411 --> 00:56:14.118
No, not really.


00:56:14.830 --> 00:56:16.821
I just need a minute, OK?
- Sure.


00:56:17.124 --> 00:56:18.580
Then we'll move on.


00:56:18.709 --> 00:56:20.416
I'll be right back.


00:56:40.731 --> 00:56:42.722
You know what always helps against grief?


00:56:43.734 --> 00:56:45.099
No.


00:56:58.248 --> 00:56:59.830
I love those!


00:57:10.802 --> 00:57:12.634
_ $0?
IS It helping?


00:57:13.889 --> 00:57:16.381
Yeah, much better already.


00:57:19.311 --> 00:57:21.143
My grandma always made these.


00:57:30.739 --> 00:57:31.729
What was that?


00:57:32.658 --> 00:57:36.117
A gentle touch.
Kills stress hormones.


00:57:37.329 --> 00:57:38.615
Yeah, right.


00:57:43.335 --> 00:57:44.416
Thank you.


00:57:47.297 --> 00:57:48.662
Shall we?


00:58:05.607 --> 00:58:09.145
So, do you have a girlfriend?
- No, not right now.


00:58:09.611 --> 00:58:12.148
My last relationship
ended three months ago.


00:58:12.322 --> 00:58:13.778
How did it end?


00:58:14.658 --> 00:58:17.150
Well, we'd "grown apart."


00:58:17.828 --> 00:58:19.410
How long were you together?


00:58:19.663 --> 00:58:20.824
Six months.


00:58:21.456 --> 00:58:23.823
Then you "grew apart" rather quickly...


00:58:26.962 --> 00:58:30.626
It was the problem I always have.
I loved her more than she loved me.


00:58:31.591 --> 00:58:34.128
Actually, I think she
didn't love me at all.


00:58:34.511 --> 00:58:35.876
From the beginning?


00:58:36.179 --> 00:58:37.669
I think so.


00:58:38.640 --> 00:58:40.677
Then why were you with her?


00:58:42.102 --> 00:58:46.221
I don't really know myself.
It happens to me again and again.


00:58:47.399 --> 00:58:49.936
I fall for women who don't fall for me.


00:58:50.694 --> 00:58:53.812
I feel at home in rejection,
as I wasn't loved enough as a child.


00:58:54.740 --> 00:58:56.697
You don't sound convinced.


00:58:57.159 --> 00:58:59.696
Ahh, I don't know.


00:58:59.703 --> 00:59:03.367
I mean yeah, my stepdad treated me like
shit, but that's way too simple.


00:59:03.957 --> 00:59:06.164
<<You have to love yourself
to be able to love others.»


00:59:06.168 --> 00:59:08.159
«Loving is easy, being
loved is difficult»


00:59:08.170 --> 00:59:10.377
Just because it's simple,
it doesn't have to be less true.


00:59:10.380 --> 00:59:12.667
I think there's something to it.


00:59:12.674 --> 00:59:16.588
Oh come on, I'll buy you a «Brigitte», it's
all in there, too. - So what?


00:59:17.429 --> 00:59:21.514
What, so what? Who on earth loves himself?
Only idiots love themselves.


00:59:21.683 --> 00:59:22.423
What?


00:59:22.601 --> 00:59:25.093
Do you know someone who loves himself?
I don't.


00:59:25.103 --> 00:59:27.720
At least nobody with more
than five brain cells.


00:59:30.525 --> 00:59:31.856
Or do you love yourself?


00:59:42.662 --> 00:59:46.781
I wasn't just at the bakery, by the way.
- Champagne?


00:59:46.958 --> 00:59:50.041
Now that we're in the Champagne...


00:59:51.338 --> 00:59:54.831
After this bottle, I'll love myself.
And all the women who love me.


00:59:56.802 --> 00:59:58.384
One can't discuss with you today.


00:59:59.137 --> 01:00:01.128
Sorry, difficult subject for me.


01:00:08.980 --> 01:00:11.312
Know what my real problem is?


01:00:12.734 --> 01:00:15.726
That I can't choose who
I fall in love with.


01:00:16.154 --> 01:00:17.986
Oh, right.
- Yeah.


01:00:18.448 --> 01:00:21.611
I keep falling in love with women
who aren't right for me.


01:00:22.661 --> 01:00:24.527
You know whose fault that is?


01:00:24.621 --> 01:00:26.953
The MHC sector of my DNA.


01:00:27.165 --> 01:00:30.533
MHC is the part that
codes the immune system.


01:00:30.710 --> 01:00:32.121
Correct.


01:00:32.712 --> 01:00:36.751
It's your field,
but I did extensive research.


01:00:36.883 --> 01:00:40.592
The MHC sees to it
that you like the smell of people...


01:00:40.720 --> 01:00:43.803
...who have an immune system
differing strongly from your own.


01:00:43.974 --> 01:00:47.433
Women can smell a
difference of a single gene!


01:00:47.811 --> 01:00:49.142
What?


01:00:51.731 --> 01:00:53.221
Take two men.


01:00:53.525 --> 01:00:59.316
One man's immune system differs from yours
by one gene more than the other's.


01:00:59.823 --> 01:01:02.030
You'll find his smell better.


01:01:02.117 --> 01:01:04.859
You can't help it, it
happens subconsciously.


01:01:06.872 --> 01:01:08.988
The biological reason is...


01:01:09.124 --> 01:01:13.709
...if you have children with someone
whose immune system is complementary...


01:01:14.171 --> 01:01:19.041
...the kids will be twice as resistant
to viruses, bacteria, etc.


01:01:19.176 --> 01:01:21.634
Evolutionary genius.


01:01:21.720 --> 01:01:28.137
That was hugely advantageous in the past
when people died like flies from infections.


01:01:29.102 --> 01:01:30.888
In the past, yes.


01:01:31.021 --> 01:01:35.891
But we no longer run around the forest in
loincloths, looking for the best-smelling DNA.


01:01:36.067 --> 01:01:38.058
Well, I do sometimes...


01:01:43.158 --> 01:01:46.696
And in terms of choosing our partners,
we're still cavemen.


01:01:46.703 --> 01:01:50.241
You know what pheromones are?
- Yes, scentless transmitting agents.


01:01:50.457 --> 01:01:55.702
Right. And most of them are located here
in the little groove above the upper lip.


01:01:55.712 --> 01:01:58.249
That's why we kiss before we mate.


01:01:58.423 --> 01:02:00.630
And tilt our heads sideways.


01:02:00.717 --> 01:02:03.049
To smell the pheromones.
- How romantic!


01:02:04.346 --> 01:02:07.134
Kissing is a gene check.
Nothing else.


01:02:08.099 --> 01:02:11.967
Thanks, now I'll always think of
"gene check" when I kiss, great.


01:02:15.982 --> 01:02:19.520
With the first kiss, you already know
if the sex will be good or not.


01:02:19.736 --> 01:02:21.067
True.


01:02:21.738 --> 01:02:26.733
And the craziest thing is: When two people
have sex who like each other's smell...


01:02:26.952 --> 01:02:30.661
...the chance that the woman gets
pregnant is three times as high.


01:02:31.873 --> 01:02:36.709
They found that out with that
T-shirt smell test. Ever heard of it?


01:02:36.878 --> 01:02:37.959
No.


01:02:39.422 --> 01:02:43.040
Ten women and ten men
wore a T-shirt for a week...


01:02:43.176 --> 01:02:46.043
...then had to select
the best-smelling one.


01:02:46.179 --> 01:02:49.388
With those who found
each other's smell appealing...


01:02:49.516 --> 01:02:53.009
...the woman was three times
more likely to get pregnant.


01:02:54.062 --> 01:02:56.144
Eww, how did they test that?


01:02:57.607 --> 01:02:59.644
I have no clue.


01:03:00.318 --> 01:03:03.310
But it doesn't work
if the woman takes the pill.


01:03:03.321 --> 01:03:06.939
Because then she prefers men
with a similar immune system.


01:03:07.117 --> 01:03:10.075
As a result, A: she won't
get pregnant as quickly...


01:03:10.161 --> 01:03:12.698
...and B: the kids will
be at the doctor all the time.


01:03:12.998 --> 01:03:17.868
So: Get off the pill six months before
marriage or your offspring is screwed.


01:03:18.086 --> 01:03:19.702
Sure thing.


01:03:21.339 --> 01:03:23.296
It actually happened to me.


01:03:23.425 --> 01:03:27.885
I dated a girl who stopped taking the pill
six months into our affair.


01:03:28.013 --> 01:03:30.050
Suddenly, we couldn't stop fighting!


01:03:30.140 --> 01:03:34.759
Because of the pill, so many couples
come together who don't match at all!


01:03:35.312 --> 01:03:39.021
Hey, we're close to Verdun.
Let's have an ice cream there.


01:03:39.190 --> 01:03:41.648
Good idea.
I want one too.


01:04:56.017 --> 01:04:59.976
Jan, about what you said earlier.
The pheromones and all.


01:05:01.606 --> 01:05:04.769
When someone blames
his relationship problems on biology,


01:05:04.943 --> 01:05:07.184
it triggers my internal alarm, because...


01:05:07.404 --> 01:05:09.145
Because it's the truth?


01:05:10.031 --> 01:05:14.696
No, kidding aside. What you're referring
to is merely sexual attraction.


01:05:15.703 --> 01:05:20.118
When two people sniff each other,
get horny and fuck, is that love?


01:05:20.375 --> 01:05:21.957
We're not animals.


01:05:22.043 --> 01:05:23.784
Sure, mammals.


01:05:23.962 --> 01:05:28.297
Nonsense! OK, I need to find a man hot
before starting a relationship with him.


01:05:28.383 --> 01:05:32.172
But that's just the first stage.
It's a great stage, yes.


01:05:32.262 --> 01:05:37.257
It's exciting, your knees go weak, you get
goosebumps and have physical reactions.


01:05:37.392 --> 01:05:41.056
But the truth is...
It's also the least interesting stage.


01:05:41.771 --> 01:05:47.813
I don't find it so uninteresting. - But
it's just unconscious, primal instincts!


01:05:48.611 --> 01:05:51.148
I mean, I've heard all those theories...


01:05:51.781 --> 01:05:56.617
...how women look for macho,
testosterone-laden men while ovulating...


01:05:56.786 --> 01:05:59.027
Like me?
- Exactly.


01:06:00.039 --> 01:06:04.374
The rest of the time, they prefer caring
types who look like their relatives.


01:06:04.461 --> 01:06:08.580
Hang on: So statistically speaking,
the caring type has an advantage?


01:06:09.215 --> 01:06:12.628
Well, now everything's clear, Jule.
- Jan, stop it!


01:06:13.136 --> 01:06:19.803
It's funny and I know those theories,
but they have no significance for your life.


01:06:19.976 --> 01:06:21.307
Why not?


