They had stable families and great sex.


01:29:48.675 --> 01:29:51.212
Because they had lovers.


01:29:51.386 --> 01:29:53.798
Both men and women.
- Really?


01:29:53.972 --> 01:29:57.340
Yeah, they thought,
"We'll give our children a stable home...


01:29:57.434 --> 01:30:00.392
...but we won't allow that
to sexually frustrate us."


01:30:00.604 --> 01:30:03.722
So they had sex whenever
and with whomever they wanted.


01:30:03.815 --> 01:30:06.853
I think that's a pretty
honest arrangement.


01:30:07.402 --> 01:30:10.110
But what if the woman fell in love
with her affair?


01:30:10.238 --> 01:30:13.105
That was a no-go.
Divorce was forbidden.


01:30:13.408 --> 01:30:15.695
And you can control that.


01:30:15.785 --> 01:30:19.403
You said it yourself:
we can decide who we fall in love with.


01:30:19.706 --> 01:30:20.992
True.


01:31:50.130 --> 01:31:52.121
That tastes so divine...


01:31:54.718 --> 01:31:57.836
I'm about to have an orgasm.
This is better than sex.


01:31:59.305 --> 01:32:02.514
Another trick to keep a marriage alive:
food instead of sex.


01:32:03.810 --> 01:32:05.050
Correct.


01:32:06.980 --> 01:32:09.938
Apropos, how's that handled
in Alex's commune?


01:32:10.734 --> 01:32:12.350
Different, I hope.


01:32:14.404 --> 01:32:18.614
Well, to be honest, they actually
do have a concept of free love there.


01:32:20.869 --> 01:32:23.327
And how did you feel about that?
You were there, right?


01:32:23.621 --> 01:32:25.032
Yes.


01:32:26.499 --> 01:32:29.491
I don't know, I was only visiting.


01:32:29.669 --> 01:32:32.377
I think it needs time.


01:32:34.340 --> 01:32:37.048
But your boyfriend was totally into it?


01:32:37.677 --> 01:32:39.714
Yeah.
He was quite enthusiastic.


01:32:40.388 --> 01:32:42.971
They had pretty girls there, after all.


01:32:46.728 --> 01:32:48.719
What?
- Nothing.


01:32:48.730 --> 01:32:50.596
I won't say anything.


01:32:50.815 --> 01:32:53.147
Join in!
They're always looking for young people.


01:32:53.943 --> 01:32:57.607
No, I don't think I'm ready
to dissolve the barriers of my ego.


01:32:58.698 --> 01:33:00.359
That I believe.


01:33:01.451 --> 01:33:04.409
And "free love" makes me
think of swinger clubs.


01:33:06.539 --> 01:33:09.406
You're a walking contradiction.
- Not at all.


01:33:09.501 --> 01:33:12.584
No. I'm not saying
everybody should bang everybody.


01:33:12.712 --> 01:33:14.953
I just say we shouldn't hold
onto monogamy...


01:33:15.131 --> 01:33:18.340
...only because state and church
propagate nuclear families.


01:33:18.635 --> 01:33:21.377
The time is ripe for new
relationship models.


01:33:23.139 --> 01:33:24.049
Yes...


01:33:25.308 --> 01:33:26.639
Maybe you're right.


01:34:03.012 --> 01:34:04.002
Morning!


01:34:04.180 --> 01:34:05.420
Morning!


01:34:05.598 --> 01:34:09.341
All good? I'm gonna take a shower.
- Okay.


01:35:15.793 --> 01:35:17.409
Wanna snitch some corn?


01:36:07.303 --> 01:36:10.637
Carla and Nicolas?
- Yes, Carla Bruni and Nicolas Sarkozy.


01:36:11.015 --> 01:36:13.598
And who is who?
Is this Carla or Nicolas?


01:36:13.685 --> 01:36:15.801
The smaller one is Nicolas.
- Of course!


01:36:32.453 --> 01:36:33.568
Smile!


01:36:37.542 --> 01:36:40.409
I feel cool, and you?


01:36:40.670 --> 01:36:42.035
You're sweating, right?


01:37:36.309 --> 01:37:38.767
Sea, we're coming!


01:38:01.667 --> 01:38:02.702
Go!


01:38:10.134 --> 01:38:11.044
Wow.


01:38:18.226 --> 01:38:20.888
Come on!
Into the sea!


01:38:30.738 --> 01:38:31.978
So nice.


01:38:36.619 --> 01:38:38.030
Come on!


01:38:44.460 --> 01:38:46.292
Come in, it's lovely!


01:39:39.974 --> 01:39:44.263
Whoa, so nice.
- Yeah.


01:39:50.276 --> 01:39:53.769
Around the University of Barcelona
so much cocaine was measured...


01:39:53.946 --> 01:39:57.280
...in the air, you would get high
just by walking around there.


01:39:59.243 --> 01:40:01.951
And those are just the Spaniards.
The Germans...


01:40:02.038 --> 01:40:04.370
...drink 500 bottles of beer a year.
Per head.


01:40:04.540 --> 01:40:05.655
500 bottles?


01:40:05.833 --> 01:40:06.823
What?


01:40:07.001 --> 01:40:09.413
And seven liters of booze.
On average, the German...


01:40:09.504 --> 01:40:11.586
...drinks twice as much
as the rest of humanity.


01:40:12.548 --> 01:40:15.165
We're a nation of full blown alcoholics.


01:40:15.259 --> 01:40:19.218
Absolutely. I mean, in fact
we're all permanently on.


01:40:19.388 --> 01:40:23.382
But why? Why do we take so many drugs?
Have you ever asked yourself that?


01:40:23.518 --> 01:40:25.008
No idea, there are a million reasons.


01:40:25.102 --> 01:40:28.686
Well... Look, in the 1950s,
there was this booze ad.


01:40:28.773 --> 01:40:32.016
Super minimalistic, only a bottle of
schnapps against a white background.


01:40:32.235 --> 01:40:34.442
And you know what was written
underneath it in capital letters?


01:40:34.445 --> 01:40:35.856
"A vacation from yourself".


01:40:36.030 --> 01:40:38.772
<<A vacation from yourself».
Cool.


01:40:39.951 --> 01:40:43.410
That's what this is all about!
Humans are the only living beings...


01:40:43.579 --> 01:40:47.038
...on this planet who can
constantly worry about themselves.


01:40:47.208 --> 01:40:50.417
About their fears, needs, deficits.
We think about the future...


01:40:50.503 --> 01:40:53.586
...about the past, what we
did right, what we did wrong.


01:40:53.589 --> 01:40:56.251
We think, think, think.
The thoughts up there...


01:40:56.342 --> 01:40:58.800
...they permanently comment
and evaluate everything you do.


01:40:58.970 --> 01:41:02.679
16 hours a day, seven days a week...
You just can't take that forever!


01:41:02.848 --> 01:41:06.762
And that is why, I say, man has
a natural need to take drugs.


01:41:06.769 --> 01:41:08.976
At least every two weeks.


01:41:09.981 --> 01:41:11.346
You, maybe...


01:41:12.608 --> 01:41:15.225
Come on, even the natives
in the jungle take drugs.


01:41:15.403 --> 01:41:17.735
Mushrooms, cacti, ayahuasca,
that sort of thing.


01:41:17.863 --> 01:41:20.776
All the peoples in the history
of mankind have taken drugs:


01:41:20.866 --> 01:41:23.574
Indians, Mayans, Incas,
Romans, Greeks, all of them!


01:41:24.412 --> 01:41:28.280
We need to get away from ourselves every
now and then. Otherwise we go crazy.


01:41:28.416 --> 01:41:33.286
Yes, but there are other ways to
take a vacation from yourself.


01:41:33.421 --> 01:41:36.254
Meditation for example, dancing, yoga!


01:41:37.300 --> 01:41:39.257
Sports, sex, anything...


01:41:39.343 --> 01:41:44.053
Yes, all right. But drugs are easier.
Open the bottle, drink, done.


01:41:44.390 --> 01:41:47.508
And human beings are lazy by nature, that's
the second principle of thermodynamics.


01:41:47.518 --> 01:41:48.974
Yes, I'm afraid so.


01:41:52.690 --> 01:41:57.400
But Jan, what if what you call
your self isn't your self?


01:41:57.778 --> 01:41:59.143
Yes?


01:41:59.322 --> 01:42:02.781
This voice in your head, constantly
commenting on what you do.


01:42:02.783 --> 01:42:04.524
I don't think that's you at all.


01:42:04.619 --> 01:42:07.577
I think that's more like
your inner commentator.


01:42:07.830 --> 01:42:08.570
What?


01:42:08.748 --> 01:42:11.536
Your inner commentator.
Like Grandpa at the Muppet Show...


01:42:11.542 --> 01:42:13.283
...who's always putting in his 2 cents?


01:42:13.461 --> 01:42:16.249
That old man with the
giant nose: Hehehehehe...


01:42:16.380 --> 01:42:22.797
Yes, that's the one. Anyway,
I think your real self is nonverbal.


01:42:22.970 --> 01:42:24.711
And it makes all the decisions.


01:42:24.805 --> 01:42:27.593
The commentator can rationalize
these decisions afterwards...


01:42:27.767 --> 01:42:29.849
...but in reality he has
nothing to say, you know?


01:42:30.561 --> 01:42:33.599
Like the commentator in a soccer
game who doesn't even play.


01:42:33.731 --> 01:42:35.597
That voice in your head,
that's not you.


01:42:36.609 --> 01:42:37.815
ORGY--...


01:42:37.943 --> 01:42:42.403
Maybe. But who am I, then?
Where is my true self located?


01:42:43.866 --> 01:42:48.656
Well, somewhere deep down,
where you can't get with language.


01:42:48.829 --> 01:42:54.370
At the core of your being, only to
be seen in dreams. I don't know...


01:42:54.502 --> 01:42:55.663
Or in psychoanalysis.


01:42:55.795 --> 01:42:57.377
Yes, maybe.


01:42:58.589 --> 01:43:03.504
Anyway, with drugs you can turn off
the commentator. But not the real you.


01:43:03.678 --> 01:43:04.759
Know what I mean?


01:43:04.762 --> 01:43:07.049
But that's awesome.


01:43:07.181 --> 01:43:08.046
What?


01:43:08.182 --> 01:43:11.595
If I can turn off the commentator.
I'll have a few hours' silence.


01:43:12.186 --> 01:43:14.598
Maybe. But with drugs
you not only turn off the...


01:43:14.689 --> 01:43:17.306
...commentator, you also
harm your true self.


01:43:17.441 --> 01:43:19.603
Look at the people who
take drugs for years.


01:43:19.735 --> 01:43:22.818
They're all totally empty at some
point, not even there any more.


01:43:23.823 --> 01:43:27.441
I mean, you know people like that, right?
- Yes, that's true.


01:43:29.036 --> 01:43:32.574
I think it's much better to
harmonize your commentator...


01:43:32.707 --> 01:43:35.290
...and your self, so that
they work as a team.


01:43:35.418 --> 01:43:38.410
Okay.
And how can I do that?


01:43:39.714 --> 01:43:42.422
I don't know.
Certainly not with drugs.


01:43:44.135 --> 01:43:45.250
How then?


01:43:50.182 --> 01:43:52.423
For example, by running
full speed to the sea...


01:43:52.601 --> 01:43:54.558
...and jumping into the
water fully dressed?


01:44:03.571 --> 01:44:04.402
Go!


01:44:42.359 --> 01:44:45.442
Sure you don't want help?
- No, it's fine.


01:44:45.946 --> 01:44:49.280
OK, then I'll take a swim.
- Have fun. See you later.


01:46:27.673 --> 01:46:28.663
Jule?


01:46:37.099 --> 01:46:38.385
Hey...


01:46:39.894 --> 01:46:40.884
Morning.


01:46:43.397 --> 01:46:44.512
Morning.


01:46:46.275 --> 01:46:47.606
This is so cool.


01:46:49.820 --> 01:46:51.606
Who gave you the wetsuit?


01:46:51.780 --> 01:46:55.398
I borrowed it from our neighbor
and thought I'd give it a try.


01:46:57.244 --> 01:46:58.655
Just round the ankle?


01:46:58.787 --> 01:47:03.247
Just round the ankle.
Okay, and now we'll paddle first.


01:47:03.375 --> 01:47:05.491
Hold the board like this.


01:47:06.879 --> 01:47:08.586
Right over there...


01:47:12.593 --> 01:47:14.550
Very good!


01:47:16.513 --> 01:47:19.175
You're doing great!
Use all of your arms strength.


01:47:21.268 --> 01:47:23.009
Back there is a nice one!


01:47:31.946 --> 01:47:34.563
Wow, super, great!


01:47:37.868 --> 01:47:39.404
Try that one.


01:47:40.287 --> 01:47:42.028
You're doing great!


01:47:43.290 --> 01:47:44.280
Yes!


01:47:45.209 --> 01:47:47.701
Gosh, that was really great!


01:47:51.256 --> 01:47:52.746
Another good one!


01:47:59.807 --> 01:48:01.047
Rad!


01:48:04.269 --> 01:48:06.761
You're really good for a beginner.


01:48:12.861 --> 01:48:16.024
You know how to surf,
You fooled me, man!


01:49:18.343 --> 01:49:21.677
Down the coast to Hossegor, Capbreton...


01:49:22.222 --> 01:49:28.889
Anglet, Biarritz, Saint Jean de Luz
and then San Sebastian.


01:49:29.605 --> 01:49:31.892
Look!
Spam!


01:49:45.245 --> 01:49:48.033
Where does your father live?
Where should I drop you off?


01:49:48.207 --> 01:49:51.541
In Zumaia, a coastal town
in the Basque Country.


01:50:52.396 --> 01:50:53.978
This is the marina.


01:51:06.451 --> 01:51:08.613
I'll check if I see him.
- Okay.


01:51:35.022 --> 01:51:36.183
And?


01:51:36.899 --> 01:51:37.980
No, he's not here.


01:51:42.196 --> 01:51:43.778
You can drive on.


01:51:46.033 --> 01:51:47.398
Sure?


01:52:19.566 --> 01:52:20.727
Is that him?


01:52:23.111 --> 01:52:24.772
Yes, that's him.


01:52:31.662 --> 01:52:33.027
Want to go over?


01:52:36.416 --> 01:52:37.326
No.


01:52:42.714 --> 01:52:45.331
Should I leave,
you want to be alone?


01:52:46.051 --> 01:52:47.212
No, no.


01:52:58.981 --> 01:53:00.813
Which of them is it?


01:53:00.983 --> 01:53:02.815
The one on the left.


01:53:16.623 --> 01:53:18.534
He looks happy, right?


01:53:19.167 --> 01:53:21.204
Definitely, yes.


01:54:13.388 --> 01:54:16.426
I don't know how to describe it.
It was...


01:54:20.062 --> 01:54:21.803
It was strange.


01:54:24.232 --> 01:54:26.564
I couldn't go over to him.


01:54:28.028 --> 01:54:30.065
I just couldn't.


01:54:32.699 --> 01:54:38.160
I didn't think it'd be such a big deal.
I thought I'd come here, see him...


01:54:40.290 --> 01:54:41.701
...we'd talk a bit.


01:54:42.709 --> 01:54:45.292
And it'd all be good, but...


01:54:47.381 --> 01:54:49.497
While standing there...


01:54:51.218 --> 01:54:54.427
I saw a stranger, not my father.


01:54:59.434 --> 01:55:01.095
And I realized...


01:55:01.645 --> 01:55:03.761
I'll never have a father.


01:55:07.859 --> 01:55:11.523
But not only a dream fell apart...


01:55:15.075 --> 01:55:17.316
I also understood something.


01:55:18.954 --> 01:55:24.620
That I have to stop looking outside of
myself, and start looking inside.


01:55:25.585 --> 01:55:28.122
Good, that's good.


01:56:53.298 --> 01:56:55.665
Beautiful, right?
- Yes.


01:56:57.260 --> 01:57:01.754
When Picasso saw this, he said we haven't
learned anything new in painting.


01:57:02.682 --> 01:57:04.798
In 25,000 years.


01:57:10.148 --> 01:57:12.856
Know why they painted mostly animals?


01:57:14.027 --> 01:57:17.395
It's assumed they worshiped
some animals like gods.


01:57:18.156 --> 01:57:22.024
They seemed so strong to them.
Elegant, superior to humans...


01:57:23.453 --> 01:57:26.195
They could only hunt
them by forming groups.


01:57:26.331 --> 01:57:27.662
Battue.


01:57:29.167 --> 01:57:31.499
Look, it's depicted there.


01:57:31.503 --> 01:57:32.584
Battue?


01:57:33.797 --> 01:57:35.333
The Cro-Magnons.


01:57:35.423 --> 01:57:37.630
That's why you brought me here.


01:57:37.717 --> 01:57:40.209
The Cro-Magnons painted these!
- Exactly.


01:57:41.513 --> 01:57:44.881
The first human who had time to do art.


01:58:04.119 --> 01:58:07.157
There they are: the Picos de Europa.


01:58:46.953 --> 01:58:49.570
Shit!
- Are you OK?


01:59:03.303 --> 01:59:05.340
And now? We run?
- Run.


01:59:05.430 --> 01:59:06.670
Run!


01:59:11.102 --> 01:59:13.013
Shit, it's so cold!


01:59:15.774 --> 01:59:17.856
Come on, get in.


01:59:21.446 --> 01:59:22.811
Everything's wet.


01:59:23.031 --> 01:59:25.238
Need a towel?
- Yes, please.


01:59:31.039 --> 01:59:34.122
Can you warm me up a bit?
- Sure. Come here.


02:00:12.080 --> 02:00:13.741
Should we really do this?


02:00:17.293 --> 02:00:18.783
Maybe we shouldn't.


02:00:32.308 --> 02:00:34.766
Damn, Jan, I...


02:00:36.438 --> 02:00:37.894
I think I...


02:00:40.442 --> 02:00:42.854
I think I'm falling in love with you.


02:00:48.533 --> 02:00:50.695
So am I.
In you.


02:00:51.119 --> 02:00:52.655
Totally.


02:01:00.420 --> 02:01:02.377
So what do we do now?


02:01:05.341 --> 02:01:06.797
Stay strong?


02:01:08.428 --> 02:01:10.135
Yeah, right?


02:01:12.390 --> 02:01:14.131
We talked about it.


02:01:17.687 --> 02:01:19.644
Says the polygamist.


02:01:19.773 --> 02:01:22.140
Polygamist, yes, but...


02:01:22.442 --> 02:01:24.228
I like it.


02:01:26.237 --> 02:01:27.773
So do I.


02:01:36.790 --> 02:01:38.701
But it's damn hard.


02:01:38.792 --> 02:01:40.282
Oh, yeah.


02:01:44.798 --> 02:01:46.584
But sniffing is OK, right?


02:01:57.393 --> 02:01:59.259
You smell incredibly good.


02:02:00.647 --> 02:02:02.263
So do you.


02:02:06.444 --> 02:02:08.276
Genetically compatible.


02:02:09.280 --> 02:02:10.441
Totally.


02:02:16.454 --> 02:02:19.446
Know what's almost better
than the kiss itself?


02:02:20.792 --> 02:02:22.874
The three seconds beforehand.


02:02:23.169 --> 02:02:25.786
The feeling when you know
it's about to happen.


02:02:32.554 --> 02:02:35.137
But we'll stay strong, right?


02:04:15.114 --> 02:04:16.445
Is everything OK?


02:04:21.996 --> 02:04:23.578
Jan, I'm pregnant.


02:04:55.321 --> 02:04:58.234
My mother wants me to get an abortion.


02:05:01.369 --> 02:05:03.451
I don't know what I want.


02:05:04.247 --> 02:05:06.238
I don't know anything anymore.


02:05:10.253 --> 02:05:11.618
Want some tea?


02:05:14.799 --> 02:05:16.164
Coming.


02:05:53.796 --> 02:05:55.207
And Alex?


02:05:55.214 --> 02:05:57.376
Does he want the child?


02:05:58.176 --> 02:05:59.291
No.


02:06:00.595 --> 02:06:02.757
"Bad timing, Jule."


02:06:10.396 --> 02:06:12.012
I can abort it with this.


02:06:14.400 --> 02:06:15.731
With pills?


02:06:15.818 --> 02:06:17.525
That works?


02:06:18.196 --> 02:06:20.187
Up until the eighth week.


02:06:22.700 --> 02:06:24.657
And what week are you in?


02:06:26.079 --> 02:06:27.569
The sixth.


02:06:27.747 --> 02:06:29.738
Not much time left.


02:07:54.083 --> 02:07:55.448
What are you making?


02:07:55.668 --> 02:07:56.783
Paella.


02:08:02.091 --> 02:08:04.332
Jan, I've made up my mind.


02:08:05.845 --> 02:08:07.961
I'm going to have the child.


02:08:16.564 --> 02:08:17.679
You think so?


02:08:17.857 --> 02:08:21.066
Of course.
You'll be a mom. That's great.


02:08:48.095 --> 02:08:49.426
I'm hungry.


02:08:50.056 --> 02:08:53.219
My child needs food.
- You can help me.


02:08:53.809 --> 02:08:54.844
Slicing onions.


02:08:55.061 --> 02:08:56.051
Good.


02:11:13.157 --> 02:11:14.443
I'm not pregnant.


02:11:15.451 --> 02:11:16.566
What?


02:11:17.453 --> 02:11:18.739
Yes...


02:11:19.455 --> 02:11:24.871
He said something like
«the egg did not stick in the uterus.»


02:11:26.879 --> 02:11:29.746
I didn't fully understand him,
his English was not so good.


02:11:31.133 --> 02:11:33.420
I was pregnant, but...


02:11:35.012 --> 02:11:37.094
It seems to happen a lot.


02:11:37.765 --> 02:11:39.130
Oh, boy.


02:11:48.859 --> 02:11:50.145
I wanna go.


02:11:50.277 --> 02:11:51.358
Sure.


02:12:57.386 --> 02:13:01.220
You know, the thought that everything
is transient is not only sad.


02:13:01.682 --> 02:13:04.094
It's also comforting.


02:13:05.644 --> 02:13:09.387
I think that's the most important thing
you have to understand in a relationship.


02:13:10.274 --> 02:13:14.142
You're with me, but you're not mine.
Nobody owns nobody.


02:13:15.613 --> 02:13:20.449
And only if I accept that it can all
be over tomorrow, I can be happy.


02:13:21.785 --> 02:13:25.449
In that moment.
With the other one.


02:14:49.873 --> 02:14:51.113
It's back on.


02:14:51.292 --> 02:14:52.327
Great.


02:15:54.271 --> 02:15:55.887
Then good luck with...


02:15:56.023 --> 02:15:57.184
Thanks.


02:16:00.861 --> 02:16:02.317
No, don't...


02:16:02.529 --> 02:16:04.111
Sorry, I...


02:16:04.740 --> 02:16:07.107
It all went so fast...


02:16:07.534 --> 02:16:08.865
So much happened.


02:16:10.871 --> 02:16:14.739
I need time to think. I need to go
to Alex. I need to talk to him.


02:16:15.876 --> 02:16:17.742
I might not come back.


02:16:24.426 --> 02:16:25.587
Jan!


02:16:29.431 --> 02:16:30.421
Lun-


02:16:39.608 --> 02:16:41.849
I have to go or I'll lose my mind.


02:17:55.100 --> 02:17:57.637
I'd like to close now.


02:18:01.398 --> 02:18:04.140
I'm closing.
- Alright.


02:18:04.401 --> 02:18:06.312
How much is it?
- Eight euros.


02:18:10.324 --> 02:18:11.405
Keep the change.


02:18:14.411 --> 02:18:16.118
Do you need a room for the night?


02:18:16.455 --> 02:18:18.162
No, thanks.


02:18:20.751 --> 02:18:22.583
I'm waiting for a woman.


02:18:23.754 --> 02:18:24.994
<i>A woman...</i>


02:18:26.256 --> 02:18:30.500
Women are our destiny. Our destiny...
- That's true.


02:18:30.844 --> 02:18:33.711
Good night.
- Good night. Thanks.

